# CITATION.cff — GitHub renders this in the repo sidebar ("Cite this
# repository") and exposes it via the GitHub citation API. Fill it so
# academic users can cite the work and Zenodo can mint a DOI later.
#
# Spec: https://github.com/citation-file-format/citation-file-format

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "StackSmith: production deployment kit for self-hosted document chat"
abstract: >-
  StackSmith is a self-hosted deployment kit for docubot, a document-grounded
  chat assistant with retrieval-augmented generation over pgvector. It packages
  the full production stack — app + worker + beat, Postgres 17 with pgvector,
  Redis, Nginx, Prometheus/Grafana/Loki/Tempo — as a single docker-compose
  deployment unit runnable on one VPS, with blue-green deploys, cosign-signed
  images, encrypted off-host backups, restore drills, and an SLO/error-budget
  model. This repository is the deployment kit; the product API it ships is
  defined in app/ and surfaced at /docs/openapi.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - pgvector
  - self-hosted
  - docker-compose
  - observability
  - blue-green-deployment
  - supply-chain-security
  - llm
authors:
